List - is supplied by an interface that has add, remove,contains,get,size,set, methods that are all meant to help build
a list.
Set - add,remove,contains,size methods.
notice set and list has common methods do we have something more general than that? Yes!,
the general collection is an interface that has add,remove,contains,size methods and the list and set interfaces extend him!

Map - maps between keys to values, contains the methods put, remove,ContainsKet,ContainsValue,get,size,keySet,values
also an interface!

the concrete classes for each one are
for list we have - ArrayList, LinkedList (theres more we will just study about them both in the course)

Set - HashSet

Map - HashMap

Iterable - the mega boss, the interface collection extends him. This interface is insane all it guarantees is that
you can just iterate it with for each loop thus you can make for each loop on all its inherits.
